title: Document preview
tags: [[file panel]]
kind: reference
aliases: pdf document documents poppler
summary: A PDF is previewed one page at a time, as an image rendered outside the application by poppler; the document itself never reaches the web view.

In the [[file panel]], a PDF is shown ''one page at a time'', as a picture of the
page. The toolbar gives the page and the count (`3 / 12`) between ''‹'' and ''›''.

|!Key |!Does |
|<<key "file:page next" PageDown>> / <<key "file:page prev" PageUp>> |next, previous page |
|`file:page first` / `file:page last` |first, last page — no key: `Home` and `End` move the list here, like the arrows |

A page being a picture, the zoom of the panel applies to it as to any image, and
turning the page keeps the zoom. In a folder's grid, and in the grid of
[[metarecord-list panel]], a PDF's tile is its first page.

The pages are rendered by ''poppler'' (`pdftoppm`, and `pdfinfo` for the count), a
separate program run in a sandbox ([[Sandboxing the media decoders]]). Without the
`poppler` package a PDF shows ''no preview available for this format'', and its tile
the 📕 glyph ([[GUI runtime dependencies]]).

Rendered pages are kept in the repository holding the file, under
`.metafolder/internal/documents/`, and a changed file is rendered again. A PDF that
is inside no loaded repository has nowhere to keep them: its page count is read, and
the page shows ''cannot render this page''.

!! Setting

`document-dpi` in `[panel-defaults.file]` ([[GUI configuration]]) is the resolution a
page is rendered at: 150 by default, a readable A4 page, and between 20 and 600.
Raise it for a sharper zoom, at the price of a slower render.

A PDF is recognised by its content, whatever its name. It is the only document
format rendered.

!! Why not the web view's own viewer

WebKit can display a PDF by itself. It is not used, because a PDF loaded as a
document would run inside the GUI's own page, with access to everything the GUI can
do ([[Why /fsraw never serves a document]]). Rendering it elsewhere and showing the
picture keeps an untrusted file out.
